It's certainly possible that these kind of game-mechanics traps are a
deliberate feature of the game, but I personally think the game would
be better if this was changed. Walking into a floating eye with no
warning and then getting killed while paralyzed is a 'trap', but it's
one that I'm happy with, because to me it makes some sense that the
character might not yet understand the potential dangers of certain
monsters, and careless actions can be costly in a dangerous dungeon.
It isn't much different from just walking into a minotaur and getting
hacked down. But with the skills thing, I feel like we're essentially
wasting good content. There's a wide array of different weapons in the
game, most of which are basically useless. I think that's a shame.

> > spear & javelin
